{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/475433-agents-being-included-with-windows-10","id":475433,"title":"Agents being included with Windows 10.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-09T23:01:11-07:00","id":475433,"title":"Agents being included with Windows 10.","content":"I remember when Trinity was launched some 18 years ago and I got my hands on the original black plastic edition. The one with AEON hidden beneath a TRINITY sticker. My friends and I played it to death. We pored over the setting details, and uncovered more mysteries with every released source book. It was a damn shame the game died, but the only good news was that it did so before it had a chance to lose focus. A bit like Firefly, maybe?<br /> <br /> One great thing about the setting was that the people who wrote it actually had spent some time thinking about how the future realistically might look in a hundred years, factoring in the Aberrants and technology. The slow but steady intrusion of the US government into monitoring and controlling its citizens, the strains on the European Union (Grexit?), the steadily increasing isolation of Japan, and the ascendancy of a China that never truly westernizes. When I read it, I didn't think I'd be sitting a decade and a half later in Shanghai writing this on a successor forum to White Wolf's dead and gone one.<br /> <br /> Anyway. The writers had a point about technology, too. At the time of Trinity's writing, mentally projecting into the Matrix was all the rage. William Gibson, then Cyberpunk RPG, then the Matrix movies. Trinity, though? Andrew Bates and the rest thought up something different. An intelligent, adaptive agent that took care of all your digital needs. Both those you request directly, and those it learns you might want or need.<br /> <br /> TechRadar has published an overview of Windows 10. It includes a section on Bill Gates' own project that will be launched as part of W10. The Personal Agent. Quoting from the text:<br /> <br /> &quot;One project I am working on with Microsoft is the Personal Agent which will remember everything and help you go back and find things and help you pick what things to pay attention to,&quot; Gates disclosed on Reddit. &quot;The idea that you have to find applications and pick them and they each are trying to tell you what is new is just not the efficient model - the agent will help solve this. It will work across all your devices.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway. End of my post. Just thought it was a fun tidbit that even if Trinity has been largely forgotten for a few years, the future it predicted is still seemingly on track. With or without Aberrants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","user":"Wintermute","date":". 04-10-2015, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","name":"Wintermute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5621_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T07:47:47-07:00","id":475817,"title":"","content":"Back around the time Aeon was being written there was a LOT of talk and experiments in the tech industry about software agents adept at information retrieval, notably through companies like Autonomy (granted they were all terrible though). Taking that idea and personalizing (even 'humanizing') the concept was, as you said, a break from the Matrix approach to network navigation that was all the rage. It is certainly fascinating to see this all start to play out, at least in one form or another <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's a direct link to the January article about the Personal Agent: <a href=\"http://www.techradar.com/us/news/world-of-tech/future-tech/bill-gates-secret-microsoft-project-is-an-advanced-personal-assistant-1282609\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.techradar.com/us/news/wor...istant-1282609</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T06:10:17-07:00","id":481282,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that, Chill. I tried linking to it in my post, but failed miserably and only managed to get to the front page of TechRadar. I really do need one of those agents.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5621-wintermute","name":"Wintermute","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5621_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T10:13:20-07:00","id":481390,"title":"","content":"No problem.<br /> <br /> On a related noted I've noticed since its last update Google Now is getting....... um........<i>chattier</i>. And a little less robotic. This thing's going to decide it doesn't need me one day......","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}